From 7952ad9141c97776701939fc8c451c19425cbb40 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yu-Cheng Chen <as95195100@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 04:12:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: realtek: load RTL826x patch firmware from
 config_init

rtl826x_probe() requests the register patch firmware and turns -ENOENT
into -EPROBE_DEFER. With the driver built in, as on filogic where
CONFIG_REALTEK_PHY=y, the PHYs probe before the root filesystem holding
rtl8261n.bin/rtl8264b.bin is mounted, so the first probe always defers.

When probe fails, phy_probe() asserts the PHY reset GPIO again. The
next attempt runs the driver's match_phy_device() before phy_probe()
releases the reset, so the RTL8261BE/RTL8261N callbacks read
PKG_MODEL/VERSION_ID from a PHY held in reset. Since the match was
tightened to require a PKG_MODEL of 0x8261, nothing matches any more
and the PHY stays unbound until phy_attach_direct() binds the generic
Clause 45 driver to it. Without the vendor patch sequence the USXGMII
link never comes up.

This breaks both 10G ports of the LTC Velo7 Max (RTL8261BE behind
reset-gpios):

  RTL8261BE 10Gbps PHY mdio-bus:06: PMA low-power suspend disabled
  RTL8261BE 10Gbps PHY mdio-bus:07: PMA low-power suspend disabled
  ...
  mtk_soc_eth 15100000.ethernet eth1: PHY [mdio-bus:06] driver [Generic Clause 45 PHY] (irq=POLL)
  mtk_soc_eth 15100000.ethernet eth2: PHY [mdio-bus:07] driver [Generic Clause 45 PHY] (irq=POLL)

Load the firmware on the first config_init() instead, as the upstream
RTL8261C_CG support does. config_init() runs when the PHY is attached
to its netdev, by which point the firmware is available, so probe no
longer defers and the reset GPIO is left alone. A missing firmware
file now fails the attach with an error message instead of silently
falling back to the generic driver.

Signed-off-by: Yu-Cheng Chen <as95195100@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/phy/realtek/phy_patch_rtl826x.c |  9 ++-------
 drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c      | 18 ++++++++++++++----
 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/phy/realtek/phy_patch_rtl826x.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/realtek/phy_patch_rtl826x.c
@@ -235,13 +235,8 @@ static int rtl826x_phy_patch_db_init(str
 
 	ret = request_firmware_direct(&fw, fw_name, dev);
 	if (ret) {
-		if (ret == -ENOENT) {
-			phydev_dbg(phydev, "Failed to request %s: defer probing\n", fw_name);
-			return -EPROBE_DEFER;
-		} else {
-			phydev_err(phydev, "Failed to request %s: %d\n", fw_name, ret);
-			return ret;
-		}
+		phydev_err(phydev, "Failed to request %s: %d\n", fw_name, ret);
+		return ret;
 	}
 
 	if (!fw->size || fw->size % sizeof(*patches) != 0) {
--- a/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
@@ -3369,10 +3369,6 @@ static int rtl826x_probe(struct phy_devi
 	phy_disable_eee_mode(phydev, ETHTOOL_LINK_MODE_5000baseT_Full_BIT);
 	phy_disable_eee_mode(phydev, ETHTOOL_LINK_MODE_10000baseT_Full_BIT);
 
-	ret = rtl826x_patch_db_init(phydev);
-	if (ret < 0)
-		return ret;
-
 	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_REALTEK_PHY_HWMON))
 		return rtl822x_hwmon_init(phydev);
 
@@ -3414,9 +3410,23 @@ static int rtl826x_config_serdes_polarit
 static int rtl826x_config_init(struct phy_device *phydev)
 {
 	const unsigned int max_dereset_tries = 5;
+	struct rtl826x_priv *priv = phydev->priv;
 	unsigned int tries = 0;
 	int ret;
 
+	/* Load the patch firmware on first use rather than from probe. When
+	 * the driver is built in, probe runs before the root filesystem is
+	 * mounted, and a deferred probe makes phylib assert the PHY reset
+	 * GPIO again. The PHY then reads back as another package model while
+	 * held in reset, no longer matches and ends up attached to the generic
+	 * Clause 45 driver.
+	 */
+	if (!priv->patch) {
+		ret = rtl826x_patch_db_init(phydev);
+		if (ret < 0)
+			return ret;
+	}
+
 	/* Suppress PHY interrupt output before the hardware reset below.
 	 * The RTL8261N asserts its interrupt pin during power-on reset, which
 	 * races with phylib registering phy_interrupt. If the IRQ fires first
